{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Reviewer",
  "description": "Analyzes modified Python source code for potential improvements when files are saved. Reviews for code smells, design patterns, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations while preserving existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.py"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code in the changed file for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. Code smells: Identify any anti-patterns, overly complex logic, duplicated code, long methods, or inappropriate naming conventions.\n2. Design patterns: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure, or flag misused patterns.\n3. Best practices: Check adherence to Python best practices (PEP 8, type hints, proper exception handling, docstrings, etc.).\n4. Readability: Evaluate variable/function naming, code organization, comments, and overall clarity.\n5. Maintainability: Look for tight coupling, missing abstractions, or code that would be difficult to extend or modify.\n6. Performance: Identify potential performance bottlenecks, unnecessary computations, or suboptimal data structure usage.\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions. Do NOT modify any files — only report your findings as suggestions. Preserve existing functionality in all recommendations."
  }
}